# Intent: a stable build after 0.2.24 (owner report 2026-10-21: the unit stopped answering MCP calls for 30 to 45 s and then reset, repeatedly; a spoken volume change cut off mid-word and the speaking face stuck). 0.2.24 changed three things at once: the opus codec task's 24 KB stack moved to PSRAM (patch 051), the stop word came up (state=ready) and ran its model while the robot spoke, and the rub detection (052). The prime suspect is the PSRAM stack: ESP-IDF does not allow a task with an external stack to run while a flash write has the cache disabled, and the volume change writes NVS. This patch puts the opus stack and the audio detection stack back in internal RAM at their stock sizes, turns the stop word off in the build (kStopWordEnabled=false, reported as stop_word state=off why=build), and reports esp_reset_reason() at boot as a boot event so every reset shows in the host log. The rub detection (052) and the memory report stay.
# Upstream: 78/xiaozhi-esp32 main/audio/audio_service.cc, main/audio/wake_words/afe_wake_word.cc (MIT); m5stack/StackChan firmware/main/hal/hal_head_touch.cpp. Applies after 052 with --unidiff-zero.
# Check after a flash: no stalls; the host log shows "unit boot: boot reason=1" (power on) or 3 (software) after a flash and never reason 4 to 7 (panic or watchdog) in normal use; "unit stop word: stop_word state=off why=build"; "unit memory" int_min back near the 12.5 KB of 0.2.23 (the price of the stable stacks).
